# {{ .Name }} ({{ .Type | title }})

Provides a certificate authority resource. Requires API version `v3.12` or higher.

Certificate authorities are used by the Bastion to validate certificates presented by devices or
users, depending on the `ca_type`: `SSH` for an SSH CA public key, or `X509` for an X.509 CA
certificate.

## Example Usage

```terraform
# An X.509 certificate authority
resource "wallix-bastion_certificate_authority" "ca_x509" {
  certificate_authority_name = "corp-x509-ca"
  ca_type                    = "X509"
  ca_certificate             = file("${path.module}/certs/corp-ca.pem")
  description                = "Corporate X.509 certificate authority"
}

# An SSH certificate authority
resource "wallix-bastion_certificate_authority" "ca_ssh" {
  certificate_authority_name = "corp-ssh-ca"
  ca_type                    = "SSH"
  ca_certificate             = file("${path.module}/certs/corp-ssh-ca.pub")
}
```

{{ .SchemaMarkdown | trimspace }}

## Import

Certificate authority can be imported using its `certificate_authority_name`, e.g.

```shell
terraform import wallix-bastion_certificate_authority.ca_x509 corp-x509-ca
```
